    <item>
      <title>Databricks: What Is That?</title>
      <link>https://hazriqpedia.github.io/posts/databricks-what-is-that/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 25 Dec 2025 18:00:14 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://hazriqpedia.github.io/posts/databricks-what-is-that/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;For a long time, &lt;strong&gt;Python + pandas&lt;/strong&gt; was more than enough for me.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Read some data, process it, send/ save the result somewhere.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Simple. Familiar. Productive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Until one day… it wasn’t.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;ndash;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;my-usual-flow-python--pandas&#34;&gt;My Usual Flow: Python + Pandas&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;My default approach was always the same:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use pandas to read data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply business logic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Push results to another system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It worked well, especially for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Small to medium datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;One-off jobs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quick experiments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’ve written backend scripts or data utilities in Python, this probably feels familiar.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>PY: defaultdict()</title>
      <link>https://hazriqpedia.github.io/posts/py-defaultdict/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 11 Jun 2025 17:13:13 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://hazriqpedia.github.io/posts/py-defaultdict/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;A &lt;code&gt;defaultdict&lt;/code&gt; is a subclass of dict that calls a factory function to supply missing values for any requested key.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;hellip;
In today&amp;rsquo;s call, I was looking at a simple python solution that will try to count the number of fruits based on types.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lets take this example. I want to know how many numbers apple in the list.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The typical way:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-python&#34; data-lang=&#34;python&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;fruit_list &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; [&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;apple&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;banana&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;apple&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;orange&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;banana&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;apple&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;]
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;fruit_counts &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; {}
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; fruit &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; fruit_list:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; fruit &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; fruit_counts:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        fruit_counts[fruit] &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;+=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;else&lt;/span&gt;:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        fruit_counts[fruit] &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;print(fruit_counts)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;# Output: {&amp;#39;apple&amp;#39;: 3, &amp;#39;banana&amp;#39;: 2, &amp;#39;orange&amp;#39;: 1}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We will check the &lt;code&gt;fruit_counts&lt;/code&gt; dict. If it&amp;rsquo;s there, add more. If not, set it it to 1.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
